tube; the profiles are its Table over the radius"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"9e3a05f7-2813-44dd-889d-9baf47ce7246"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A region on a graph is measured by counting vertices, and its boundary is \
not negligible at a finite scale: the vertices at distance exactly ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "62e3204b-a85a-4c07-b4b7-2bb94d308ca6"],
 " are a share of order ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "/", 
   StyleBox["r", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "beb310ec-e42a-4376-90e5-78486baf4151"],
 " of the ball of radius ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ce870d5a-61ac-474c-ad01-30d5c1ddc431"],
 ". So every region carries two measures. The counting measure is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["\[Mu]", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     StyleBox["A", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}]}], "=", 
   TemplateBox[{
     StyleBox["A", "TI"]},
    "Abs"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a4e46d47-8491-4aef-8fd8-46eb6b73aed7"],
 ". The Riemannian measure is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Mu]", "TI"], "\[SmallCircle]"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     StyleBox["A", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}]}], "=", 
   TemplateBox[{
     SuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["A", "TI"], "\[SmallCircle]"]},
    "Abs"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0b126a1f-92df-4ccd-8983-3b9c78ff7d18"],
 ", where ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["A", "TI"], "\[SmallCircle]"], "=", "{", 
    StyleBox["v", "TI"], "\[Element]", 
    StyleBox["A", "TI"]}], ":", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["N", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["v", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "\[SubsetEqual]", 
    StyleBox["A", "TI"], "}"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "08cde7ff-f53f-41ea-9d25-ca2fd8056f63"],
 " is the set of vertices all of whose neighbours lie in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["A", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "367fd77b-4e95-4819-b5a3-d186afbe2408"],
 "; it is the count without the boundary and the default of the growth \
estimators."
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"c5c4f7c6-5cf4-4473-a329-ab937e169e73"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "On the square grid the ball of radius ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a2915300-c96d-4ef9-99fb-34afa1baf9d3"],
 " has counting measure ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["r", "TI"], "2"], "+", "2", 
   StyleBox["r", "TI"], "+", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0c84b7e1-fa63-4004-b8ef-b550b1b45bd1"],
 " and Riemannian measure ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["r", "TI"], "2"], "-", "2", 
   StyleBox["r", "TI"], "+", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "99bd7043-c22c-4cab-bba3-ed28a5f176b0"],
 ", the counting measure of the ball of radius ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["r", "TI"], "-", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "dfb3d5c5-0d4c-4160-b897-2013022d3a63"],
 "; the shell has counting measure ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"4", 
   StyleBox["r", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7a62b3fb-f79a-4adb-ad8f-7310c0a09359"],
 " and Riemannian measure ",
 Cell[BoxData["0"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "261e3eaf-b2c1-4895-9c7f-3b5d26cbe04e"],
 ". The same shift holds on the triangular lattice before the rim, the \
convention of the Wolfram Physics technical introduction."
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"21defabc-1409-43b2-9c30-8132822d876a"],

